{"type":"user","uuid":"e0aec50e-462e-4b61-80d9-5b206b536bde","parentUuid":"6bb5a486-6864-4971-8410-8c1942c98dd3","isSidechain":false,"timestamp":"2026-10-06T02:17:41.894Z","sessionId":"316e29ab-bac0-4164-bd11-eca051806591","version":"2.1.290","cwd":"<clone>","message":{"role":"user","content":"The usage line doubles the square brackets for optional arguments whose type already puts brackets around its metavar. For example `@click.argument(\"method\", type=click.Choice([\"foo\", \"bar\", \"baz\"]), nargs=-1)` shows `Usage: cli [OPTIONS] [[foo|bar|baz]]...` instead of `[foo|bar|baz]...`, and an optional `click.DateTime(formats=[\"%Y-%m-%d\"])` argument shows `[[%Y-%m-%d]]`. Fix it so these get a single pair of brackets without changing how other arguments are shown, and add a regression test. The existing tests must keep passing."}}
